# Direct runtime dependencies, exact pins. This is the file a human edits;
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from it -- with `uv pip compile --universal`,
# not bare pip-compile -- and carries every transitive dependency with sha256
# hashes for every platform, so `pip install --require-hashes -r
# requirements.txt` (what scripts/redeploy.sh runs on the Mini on every
# deploy, and what CI runs) installs exactly the bytes that were tested --
# not whatever a floor, an unpinned transitive, or a tampered release would
# resolve to that day. --universal matters: a plain `pip-compile` (pip-tools)
# resolves environment markers against the machine that ran it and silently
# drops a package a DIFFERENT platform needs -- this bit us for real: compiling
# on an arm64 Mac omitted SQLAlchemy's platform-gated `greenlet` dependency
# entirely, and CI's x86_64 Linux runner then failed --require-hashes outright
# ("all requirements must have their versions pinned with =="). uv's
# --universal keeps every platform's branch and hashes it. Bump a pin here,
# then regenerate:
#
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt requirements.in
#
# Dependabot understands this layout and regenerates requirements.txt itself
# in its PRs. See CONTRIBUTING.md's "Dependencies".
